Licensing for the Accountable AI Software Factory Companion Repository

This repository contains two distinct kinds of work, licensed differently.

================================================================================

1. WRITTEN CONTENT — Creative Commons BY-NC-SA 4.0
   See: LICENSE-CONTENT

   Applies to:
     templates/         Reader decision and operating instruments
     reference-factory/ Architecture contracts, traces, and acceptance suite,
                        except executable code named below
     Any prose, README, or creative work in this repository.

   Summary:
     Free for non-commercial use. Attribution required. Derivative works
     must be shared under the same license. Commercial use — including
     paid courses, paid SaaS products bundling these artifacts, or using
     them as training data for commercial AI — requires separate written
     permission from the author.

================================================================================

2. EXECUTABLE SOURCE CODE — MIT License
   See: LICENSE-CODE

   Applies to:
     reference-factory/example/*.py
     reference-factory/run-reader-journey.sh
     Executable source files that explicitly carry the MIT license.

   Summary:
     Standard MIT terms. Use, fork, modify, integrate into commercial
     or non-commercial projects freely, with attribution per the MIT
     notice.

================================================================================

WHY THE SPLIT

The written content, templates, contracts, workbooks, traces, and acceptance
suite are the intellectual contribution of the book *The Accountable AI
Software Factory*. They are offered freely for individual
readers and non-commercial adoption — that is the spirit of a book
companion repository — but it is not offered for commercial repackaging
without acknowledgment of the source.

The executable code is offered under MIT because that is the universal
convention for technical book companion code; readers and teams should
be able to drop these examples into their own projects without license
friction.

This dual-licensing arrangement is consistent with practices used by
other technical book authors who want their code freely reusable while
preserving control over the commercial use of their written work.

================================================================================

QUESTIONS

For commercial licensing inquiries — speaking engagements, paid
workshops based on these materials, enterprise training contracts that
include these templates as deliverables, or AI training data licensing —
contact the author directly.

